From afbb238864532be5df730d9fba70606fea85c64c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:15:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/52] vulkan: MMVQ fast path for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/IQ4_XS with
 hoisted per-thread chunk decoding

Each thread owns a fixed 16-value (K-quants) or 32-value (IQ4_XS) chunk of
every superblock it visits, so block/scale indices, shifts and masks are loop
invariant; weights of a row are unpacked once and reused for all columns, and
the q8_1 activations of a column are loaded once per superblock for all rows.
The thread->data mapping and per-thread accumulation order are unchanged, so
results are bit-identical to the previous kernel (checked on model shapes and
greedy llama-server output). RDNA3/4: IQ4_XS uses 2 rows per workgroup above
four columns.

RX 7900 XTX (RADV), n=6, chained matvec bench (us):
  q5_K 17408x5120 88.2->84.6, 5120x17408 90.4->88.4
  q4_K 17408x5120 80.7->75.6, 5120x17408 70.7->65.0, 10240x5120 49.1->44.8
  iq4_xs 17408x5120 85.0->77.4, 5120x17408 77.7->64.4
llama-bench pp6 (d=0): 31.95 -> 30.43 ms
